      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-08-14_WidnesExaminer_art0023" n="art0023">
        <head>NOTES ON GAMES AND ATHLETICS.</head>
        <p>NOTES ON GAMES AND ATHLETICS.</p>
        <p>Cricket.</p>
        <p>Warrington had a relaxation from League cricket on Saturday and . beautiful weather favoured their match at Wigan. The Warringtonians lacked the valuable help of, the Rev. H. Gray, W. 11. Podmore and J. W. Pearson; and the bowling was chiefly shared by H. Callon,. B. Silcock and Cresswell. Wigan were in a scoring mood and declared their innings after amassing the fine total of 205 for seven wickets. Broughton, who has played for Lincolnshire in the Minor Counties Competition, gave a brilliant batting display, and had knocked up 49 when he was magniti- .cently caught on the boundary by Wright. ,S. G. Urmson was another very successful batsman, his total beinc, 41. Warrington had two .hours in which to save the game and they managed to do So, their innings realizing 131 for 7 wickets.</p>
        <p>B. Silcock, the Warrington captain, was in good form with the bat and contributed an invaluable 37. H. Speakman, a promising young amateur, acquitted himself surprisingly well and placed 26 to his credit.</p>
        <p>Warrington 2nd met Wigan 2nd at Arpley in a</p>
