      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-08-14_WidnesExaminer_art0024" n="art0024">
        <p>The Examiner, Saturday, August 14, 1909</p>
        <p>succeeded Shaw bowled with coolness and accuracy and won by 15-13. One of the surprises of the after loon was the trounc- ing which A. Gleave experiencei at the Lands of It. Knight. The latter led from the third End and GleaVe had not a look-in, Knight piling on the nice margin of 11 One of those games which keep the _spectator on.</p>
        <p>I'. Newton</p>
        <p>J. Shaw R. Knight . 15 A. Gletve A. Stringer.. .1. Woods l4 Ted Gletve W. Daniels l5 W. Jonei G. Shaw 158 U 2 Majority for Rylands'S 16. Mr. J. Willett ably discharged the duties of referce. THE SPEN.CHES. .</p>
