      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-08-14_WidnesExaminer_art0065" n="art0065">
        <head>FIFTH TEST MATCH.</head>
        <p>THE FIFTH TEST MATCH.</p>
        <p>' The fifth and last Test match at the Oval was favoured with brilliant weather, and for once in a way the Australians had nothing to grumble it. The heat was quite Antipodean, and while the En;lishmen endured it with all the patience they could muster the Colonials seemed quite happy. Mr. Noble won the toss for the fifth time, and thus equalled the Hon. F. S. Jackson's record of 1905 when he beat Mr. Darling in the choice of innings Hi each of the five Test games. Our photographs show Mr. W. Bardsley (left-hander) whq Scored 136 in Australia's first innings, and Mr. VictQr Trumper whose 76 is his highest contribution to the present series of Test matches.</p>
      </div>
