      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-08-14_WidnesExaminer_art0126" n="art0126">
        <head>NEXT WEEK'S PROGRAMME.</head>
        <p>NEXT WEEK'S PROGRAMME.</p>
        <p>" The Man ort the Box" which comes direct from the Marlborough Theatre London and is presented by Mr. Dore Davidson's London Company, will be the attraction at the Royal Court 'Theatre next week. The play has the reputation of being very funny and has met with considerable success not only in London and the towns as yet visited, but also in America, where it is now in its forth season. A company of recognised West End artistes appear in the cast, foremost amongst whom, are Miss Rose Temple and Mr. Charles Leveson Lane. In the one act play entitled "A Dance at Dawn" an episode in "The Reign of Terror" which precedes " The Man on the Box" a great treat is in store, in the dancing of an English Prima Ballerina, Mlle. Dolli, late of the Verdi Theatre, and La Scala Theatre, whose Milanese, Eastern and Russian Dances, at the Midsummer Fete at Olympia last June were greatly admired by H.M. the Queen, before whom Mlle. Dolli had the distinguished honour of dancing on three occasions.</p>
      </div>
